# UI Testing Patterns

## Page Object Model (E2E)

E2E tests MUST use Page Object Model. Each page/screen gets a class encapsulating locators and interactions.

```typescript
// GOOD: Page Object
class LoginPage {
  readonly usernameInput = this.page.getByLabel('Username');
  readonly passwordInput = this.page.getByLabel('Password');
  readonly submitButton = this.page.getByRole('button', { name: /log in/i });

  constructor(private readonly page: Page) {}

  async login(username: string, password: string) {
    await this.usernameInput.fill(username);
    await this.passwordInput.fill(password);
    await this.submitButton.click();
  }
}
```

**Page Object rules:**
- Locators only — NO assertions inside page objects
- Public methods describe user intent (`login`, `search`), not UI actions (`clickButton`)
- Keep thin — extract shared fragments (nav, toolbar) into separate objects

## Component Testing

Test user-visible behavior, not implementation details.

```typescript
// GOOD: test what the user sees and does
test('shows error when email is invalid', async () => {
  render(<EmailForm />);
  await userEvent.type(screen.getByLabelText('Email'), 'not-an-email');
  await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /submit/i }));
  expect(screen.getByText(/invalid email/i)).toBeVisible();
});

// BAD: testing implementation details
test('sets error state', () => {
  const { container } = render(<EmailForm />);
  expect(container.querySelector('.error')).toBeTruthy();
});
```

- Use `screen.getByRole/LabelText/TestId` (not `container.querySelector`)
- Use `@testing-library/user-event` (not `fireEvent`)
- Wrap providers (router, context, i18n) in a custom `render` function

## API Mocking

Mock at the network level, not the module level.

```typescript
// GOOD: MSW at the network level
import { http, HttpResponse } from 'msw';
import { setupServer } from 'msw/node';

const server = setupServer(
  http.get('/api/users', () => HttpResponse.json([{ id: 1, name: 'Alice' }])),
);

beforeAll(() => server.listen());
afterEach(() => server.resetHandlers());
afterAll(() => server.close());
```

- MSW for integration tests (Vitest + jsdom/node)
- Page/Context route interception for E2E tests (Playwright `page.route()`)
- Share handler definitions between tests — don't duplicate

## Fixture Factories

Prefer factory functions over static JSON fixtures.

```typescript
// GOOD: factory with defaults + overrides
function createUser(overrides?: Partial<User>) {
  return {
    id: 1,
    name: 'Default User',
    email: 'default@example.com',
    role: 'viewer',
    ...overrides,
  };
}

// Use in tests
const admin = createUser({ role: 'admin' });
```

- Factories compose: `createUser(createProfile())` for related entities
- Overrides are explicit — test intent is clear
- No magic defaults that change meaning between tests

## Data Cleanup

Each test leaves the environment clean.

- E2E: use `project.dependencies` in Playwright config for setup/teardown projects
- Integration: `afterEach` resets MSW handlers and mocks
- Component: unmount + cleanup is automatic with Testing Library + Vitest
